WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:04.640
Phillip: Poor communication has a wide
range of negative effects for all types

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:08.680
of workplaces, so let’s look at some
of the possible impacts in detail.

00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:11.000
Maddy: Damage to timelines

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:15.130
If there is ineffective communication
in the workplace, people won’t

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:16.279
know what the deadlines are.

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:22.860
These can lead to increased time pressures and
possibly sloppy work, as people race to hit

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:25.210
deadlines, or deadlines are missed altogether.

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:28.180
This will almost always have a knock-on effect.

00:00:28.939 --> 00:00:33.769
Say, for example, due to poor communication,
someone in the IT department of a company

00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:38.140
is under the impression, that a new system
doesn’t need to be put in place for a month.

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:43.460
They then learn it is business critical and
must be finished before the end of the week!

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:49.840
Even if it is completed on time, it’s more than
likely it will not be executed to a good standard.

00:00:50.290 --> 00:00:53.949
And the person working on it, will
have experienced unnecessary stress

00:00:53.949 --> 00:00:56.290
and anxiety and felt highly pressured.

00:00:57.580 --> 00:00:59.110
Phillip: Reduced productivity

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:04.110
As poor communication is likely to mean
that people don’t always know what they’re

00:01:04.110 --> 00:01:09.590
expected to be doing, some may put their
energy and resources into the wrong places.

00:01:10.469 --> 00:01:13.470
They might start work on something
that’s being worked on by someone

00:01:13.480 --> 00:01:15.880
else or has already been completed.

00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:22.330
They may misunderstand a business need and create
something that doesn’t meet the goals and targets.

00:01:23.210 --> 00:01:27.820
They may even think that there’s nothing to do
that day, because no one’s told them otherwise!

00:01:29.389 --> 00:01:31.510
Maddy: Competing communication styles

00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:35.940
Although everyone has their preferred
method of communication, and that’s fine!

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:39.810
- there does still need to be some common
understanding throughout a workplace,

00:01:40.190 --> 00:01:41.869
about how people should communicate.

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:46.229
People need to know what channels to use,
and the tone of voice they’re expected to

00:01:46.230 --> 00:01:50.399
use in written and spoken communication
especially with customers, and such.

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:56.680
Without this, you’ll find that people just use
whatever channel or style they prefer, which

00:01:56.680 --> 00:01:59.050
may not be the most suitable or efficient one.

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:05.380
For example, a manager who hates to use
phone or video calls, only communicates

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:07.600
via emails and instant messaging.

00:02:08.270 --> 00:02:13.940
This might lead his team to feel very distant from
him, like he isn’t in the loop and doesn’t care.

00:02:14.770 --> 00:02:16.390
This will then be bad for their morale.

00:02:17.679 --> 00:02:20.279
Phillip: Lack of engagement and lowered wellbeing

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:24.829
Poor communication may also mean
that people don’t feel like they

00:02:24.829 --> 00:02:26.950
belong to their team or organization.

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:32.850
They’ll feel isolated, lonely, and
their morale will be low, so causing an

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:35.140
impact on productivity and retention.

00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:36.590
Maddy: Closed minds

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:43.310
Without open and effective lines of communication
between people and teams, employees won’t be

00:02:43.330 --> 00:02:46.040
regularly exposed to new ideas and approaches.

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:52.420
This can mean that inefficient methods don’t get
corrected and that problems don’t get solved.

00:02:53.620 --> 00:02:54.670
Phillip: Poor retention

00:02:55.639 --> 00:02:59.179
Without effective communication helping
people to feel like they’re a part of

00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:03.519
their organization, there will be a reduced
desire to be loyal to their employer.

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:09.030
They won’t feel like their contributions are
being noticed or their ambitions respected.

00:03:09.670 --> 00:03:14.869
This means it will be much harder to retain
talent and time and money will be spent having to

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:21.320
hire new employees, to replace the ones who go,
possibly starting the whole process over again.

00:03:22.050 --> 00:03:27.629
Maddy: Ineffective or poor communication in the
workplace can be frustrating at all levels and

00:03:27.630 --> 00:03:33.350
can create a breeding ground for mistrust and
confusion and help create stressed employees.

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:38.100
It also makes it difficult for people to
work together closely, collaboratively,

00:03:38.350 --> 00:03:39.800
and successfully as a team.

00:03:40.540 --> 00:03:44.420
This can then impact greatly on the
success of the business or organization

00:03:44.420 --> 00:03:50.690
overall, lowering morale and motivation and
ultimately affecting a businesses reputation.

